@startuml Benchmark_Sequence_Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20

actor User #lightgreen
participant "Orchestrator" as Orchestrator #lightyellow
participant "Benchmark\nRunner" as BenchmarkRunner #lightblue
participant "Main Node" as MainNode #lavender
participant "RabbitMQ" as RabbitMQ #wheat
participant "Worker" as Worker #lightcyan
participant "Analyzer" as Analyzer #pink

title BRISE Benchmark - High-Level Flow

== 1. Initialization ==
User -> Orchestrator: **Start Benchmark**\n//./init.sh up benchmark//
activate Orchestrator
Orchestrator -> BenchmarkRunner: run_benchmark()
activate BenchmarkRunner

== 2. Execute Experiments ==
loop For each experiment

    BenchmarkRunner ->> MainNode: **Start Experiment** (sync)\n//perform_experiment()//
    activate MainNode
    MainNode -->> BenchmarkRunner: ✓ Acknowledged\n//{'status': 'running'}//
    note right of MainNode: Synchronous:\nRequest-Response

    loop Optimization iterations
        MainNode -> MainNode: **Select configurations**\n//ConfigurationSelection//
        MainNode ->> RabbitMQ: **Publish tasks**\n//task_queue//
        activate RabbitMQ
        RabbitMQ ->> Worker: **Dispatch task**
        activate Worker
        note right of Worker: Asynchronous:\nEvent-driven
        Worker -> Worker: **Run experiments**\n//worker_method()//
        Worker ->> RabbitMQ: **Publish results**\n//task_result_exchange//
        deactivate Worker
        RabbitMQ ->> MainNode: **Deliver results**
        deactivate RabbitMQ
        MainNode -> MainNode: **Update model**\n//add_configuration()//
    end

    MainNode ->> RabbitMQ: **Publish completion event**\n//final_event()//
    activate RabbitMQ
    RabbitMQ -->> BenchmarkRunner: **Experiment complete** (async)
    deactivate RabbitMQ
    note left: Async notification\nwhen done

    BenchmarkRunner ->> MainNode: **Download results** (sync)\n//download_latest_dump()//
    MainNode -->> BenchmarkRunner: ✓ Results file\n//experiment.pkl//
    deactivate MainNode
    BenchmarkRunner -> BenchmarkRunner: **Store results**\n//./results/serialized///

end

BenchmarkRunner ->> MainNode: **Stop** (sync)\n//stop_main()//
activate MainNode
MainNode -> RabbitMQ: **Disconnect & cleanup**
activate RabbitMQ
RabbitMQ --> MainNode: ✓ Disconnected
deactivate RabbitMQ
MainNode -->> BenchmarkRunner: ✓ Stopped
deactivate MainNode
deactivate BenchmarkRunner

== 3. Analysis ==
BenchmarkRunner -->> Orchestrator: ✓ All experiments complete
participant "Config\nDetector" as ConfigDetector #thistle
participant "Interactive\nBaseline Analyzer" as InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer #orchid
participant "Baseline\nSelection UI" as BaselineSelectionUI #lightcyan
participant "Comparative\nOrchestrator" as ComparativeOrchestrator #lightsteelblue
participant "Report/Export\nService" as ReportService #lightgray

Orchestrator -> ConfigDetector: **Detect benchmark config**\n//detect_config_file()//
ConfigDetector -->> Orchestrator: config path
Orchestrator -> ConfigDetector: **Load + inspect config**\n//load_config(), has_comparative_analysis()//
ConfigDetector -->> Orchestrator: config dict + comparative mode flag

alt Interactive baselines enabled AND comparative analysis active
    Orchestrator -> InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer: **analyze_with_baseline_selection()**
    activate InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer

    alt Previous baseline selection exists
        InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer -> InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer: **Reuse baseline_selection.json**
    else No saved selection
        InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer -> Analyzer: **Load experiments for UI choices**
        Analyzer -->> InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer: selectable experiments
        InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer -> BaselineSelectionUI: **Start local server + render selection page**
        BaselineSelectionUI -> User: **Open browser**\n//http://localhost:8765//
        User -> BaselineSelectionUI: **Select baseline experiments**
        BaselineSelectionUI -->> InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer: selected baseline names
        InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer -> InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer: **Persist baseline_selection.json**
    end

    InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer -> ComparativeOrchestrator: **Register user baselines**
    InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer -> Analyzer: **Run analyzer with selected baselines**
    deactivate InteractiveBaselineAnalyzer
else Standard analysis path
    Orchestrator -> Analyzer: **Analyze results**\n//BenchmarkAnalyzer.analyze()//
end

activate Analyzer

loop For each objective partition
    Analyzer -> Analyzer: **Generate plots + summary table**
    note right of Analyzer
      Improvement/custom/box plots
      Grouping + normalization
      Known-optimum overlay (optional)
    end note
end

alt Comparative analysis configured
    Analyzer -> ComparativeOrchestrator: **Compute comparative metrics**
    ComparativeOrchestrator -->> Analyzer: comparative results per objective
    Analyzer -> Analyzer: **Generate comparative plots + performance profile**
end

Analyzer -> ReportService: **Export CSV/ZIP + render HTML report**
ReportService -->> Analyzer: benchmark_report.html + download artifacts
Analyzer -> User: **Open HTML report**
deactivate Analyzer
deactivate Orchestrator

User -> User: **Review results**

@enduml
